WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.402 line:90%
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:07.510 line:90%
 Hey, everyone.

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:10.690 line:10%
I'm here at Marvel Studios with
the head of visual development,

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:11.490 line:10%
Ryan Meinerding.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.390 line:90%
Hello, sir.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.190 line:90%
 Hello.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.460 line:84%
 I wish we could
go to your office,

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.530 line:84%
but apparently it's
full of spoilers?

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:19.470 line:84%
 There's a lot of stuff on the
walls that people can't see.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.120 line:84%
 Well, I have an NDA,
so I'm going to find out

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.070 line:84%
all the secrets after
this interview when

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.240 line:90%
the cameras aren't rolling.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.460 line:84%
But for now, let's
talk about Mysterio.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.190 line:84%
When me and the rest of
the fans saw the trailer,

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:34.230 line:84%
we were like holy smokes, that
is one big, swashbuckling,

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:37.050 line:90%
heroic looking Mysterio.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.960 line:84%
And he has a pretty
kind of fun campy

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.910 line:90%
origin story in the comics.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.460 line:84%
So how do you start
to play with that

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.160 line:90%
in turning it into that look?

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.740 line:84%
 With his look from the comics,
because it's essentially--

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.190 line:84%
in some version, it's
more like a green onesie.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:52.990 line:90%
LORRAINE CINK: Yeah.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:54.180 line:84%
RYAN MEINERDING: The
idea of it being more

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.147 line:84%
of a classic superhero suit
meant we were looking at things

00:00:56.147 --> 00:00:57.300 line:90%
we've done for Vision--

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.700 line:84%
just saying, OK, how
could we translate

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.180 line:84%
that into something that
was reasonable for Mysterio?

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:04.514 line:84%
 See, now that you've said
it's a onesie, all I can wonder

00:01:04.514 --> 00:01:06.320 line:84%
is if it has little
buttons in the back.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.410 line:90%
[LAUGHING]

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.343 line:10%
RYAN MEINERDING: It doesn't.

00:01:08.343 --> 00:01:09.730 line:84%
It has a zipper
somewhere, but no--

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:10.530 line:90%
no buttons.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.060 line:90%
 It's Mysterio-ous, though.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.110 line:90%
 Yeah, very nice.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:13.950 line:90%
[LAUGHING]

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.350 line:84%
 One of the things we do
just to automatically make

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.290 line:84%
something feel more
real in some ways

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.230 line:90%
is just to make it metallic.

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:21.030 line:90%
[LAUGHING]

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:24.450 line:84%
I mean, the second you use a
metallic paint on his suit,

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.630 line:90%
it just feels more real.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:28.170 line:90%
It gives life to the--

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.270 line:84%
when he's moving around, there's
reflections playing off of it,

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.430 line:84%
and it just doesn't
feel dead or flat.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.500 line:84%
 He's got such
a long comic book

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.710 line:90%
history from way back in 1964.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:41.400 line:84%
Where did you start with
those original Ditko drawings

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.990 line:90%
and bring it into today?

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:46.440 line:84%
 I mean, I always love looking
back at the old artwork.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.480 line:84%
The older it is, the better,
because it usually starts

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.560 line:90%
from such a unique place.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.770 line:84%
And that's one of the reasons
why MCU characters tend to end

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.430 line:90%
up looking sort of more unique.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:57.780 line:84%
With the Ditko stuff, I
mean, he drew hands so well,

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:58.950 line:90%
and he also--

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:01.380 line:84%
the weirdness of the
characters really came through,

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.230 line:84%
whether it was in Spider-Man or
Mysterio or in Doctor Strange--

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:07.080 line:84%
and then also just, the main
icon being that fishbowl.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.250 line:10%
Like, how can we
get that in there

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:10.793 line:10%
and-- and have it
not look goofy?

00:02:10.793 --> 00:02:12.660 line:84%
LORRAINE CINK: Well, and
that's an interesting question,

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.160 line:84%
too, because one of
the things I always

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.017 line:84%
think about-- that fishbowl look
in the comics-- it's so cool.

00:02:17.017 --> 00:02:18.750 line:84%
But you're like, how does
he get his head in there--

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:19.550 line:90%
 Right.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.030 line:84%
 --if it is a
perfectly round sphere?

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.410 line:90%
So how do you solve for that?

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.503 line:84%
 So we were actually
trying to do that.

00:02:25.503 --> 00:02:26.670 line:84%
We were seeing if
early on it would

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.080 line:84%
be better if we
turned it into more

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.720 line:84%
of an actual
head-friendly shape.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.970 line:84%
And then you do it, and it just
doesn't look like Mysterio.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:35.520 line:10%
And that's one of the things
that, when you start down

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.040 line:10%
these roads of-- of
looking at what was done

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.320 line:10%
in the past from the comics
and seeing how to translate it

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.270 line:10%
for a screen, there's
so many problems

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:43.470 line:10%
that are solved for
us that we don't

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.770 line:10%
necessarily even register.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:49.650 line:84%
So I tried to do other versions
of the big fishbowl head

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.300 line:84%
without the cloak
or a smaller cloak,

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.820 line:90%
and it just doesn't work.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.970 line:84%
Ditko got it right
the first time.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:58.800 line:84%
 There's so many fun little
details from the comics that

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.390 line:90%
always appear in the films.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.670 line:84%
I'm a huge comic
book reader and fan,

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.920 line:90%
I know our fans are as well.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.730 line:84%
Do you have maybe three
little Easter eggs for us

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.070 line:84%
that you can tell us from
the original visual design?

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.200 line:90%
 For Mysterio, specifically?

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.670 line:90%
 Mm-hmm.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:18.070 line:84%
 I mean, I think working
in eyes as many places

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:18.870 line:90%
as we could--

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:22.080 line:84%
I think we got them
here on the clasps.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.020 line:84%
They're in his-- when
he uses his powers,

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.350 line:84%
there's sort of a triangle
with an eye in it.

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:31.140 line:84%
There's other very
subtle things that I

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:35.000 line:84%
don't know if you would really
want to see them if you--

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:35.800 line:90%
 But w--

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:36.600 line:90%
[LAUGHING]

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:37.560 line:90%
 I want to know.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.360 line:84%
 If you look at
something like--

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.620 line:84%
classic superhero
costumes usually

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.640 line:84%
have some version of a letter--
a symbol or a letter on it.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:43.440 line:90%
 Yeah.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.630 line:84%
 Mysterio doesn't in
the comics, typically,

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.520 line:90%
other than the eye clasps--

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.120 line:90%
sort of did that to Mysterio.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.020 line:84%
There's a bunch of vertical
bands around his stomach

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.120 line:84%
that are essentially
Ms that are repeating.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.200 line:90%
LORRAINE CINK: I love that.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.400 line:84%
RYAN MEINERDING:
It's very subtle,

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.545 line:84%
and once you see it you
can't unsee it, so beware.

00:03:59.545 --> 00:04:00.345 line:90%
[LAUGHING]

00:04:00.345 --> 00:04:01.650 line:90%
 OK.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:05.820 line:84%
Also, I want to say that
you took a bold move

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:08.480 line:90%
and you gave Mysterio a beard.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.250 line:84%
What's-- what's up
with bearded Mysterio--

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:10.860 line:84%
RYAN MEINERDING:
Bearded Mysterio.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:11.370 line:84%
LORRAINE CINK:
--besides the fact

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.200 line:84%
that Jake Gyllenhaal
looks great with a beard?

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.010 line:84%
 I think a lot of it has
to do with Jake Gyllenhaal

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:16.130 line:90%
looking great with a beard.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:16.930 line:90%
 OK.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:20.089 line:84%
 I mean, in a lot
of ways, this movie

00:04:20.089 --> 00:04:23.250 line:84%
is Peter trying to come to
terms with being his own hero

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:25.230 line:84%
and not living
under Tony's shadow.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:27.480 line:84%
And I think having
another mentor

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:32.100 line:84%
that also had a goatee also is
a symbol of age, in some ways--

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.720 line:90%
being seasoned in the world.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:36.660 line:84%
And I-- and more directly
relating it to Tony,

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.670 line:84%
I think that connection
is great to have visually.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:42.300 line:84%
 I got to view some
of your iterations

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.970 line:90%
of the Mysterio entire design.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.190 line:84%
How many iterations do you
think you went through?

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.390 line:84%
RYAN MEINERDING:
Probably-- he's one

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:49.470 line:84%
of those characters
who can go in a lot

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.270 line:90%
of different directions.

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:52.290 line:84%
Any of the characters
that really have

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:57.330 line:84%
a very unique and
interesting origin visual

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.280 line:84%
means that when you translate
it to in a story world

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.260 line:84%
that needs to be more
realistic, it needs to be

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.580 line:90%
grounded in something else.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:03.450 line:90%
So we've-- I don't know.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:06.360 line:84%
I probably tried between
60 and 70, I think.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.690 line:84%
It took about that many
to get through, um,

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:12.610 line:84%
for the producers and Jon
to really feel like it--

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:13.830 line:90%
it was working.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.090 line:84%
One of the best
parts of this job

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:18.230 line:84%
is really being able to work
with amazing filmmakers and--

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.910 line:84%
and turn their
ideas into something

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:24.870 line:84%
that's real based on the comic
origins of the characters.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.540 line:84%
Marvel Studios is
unique in, you know,

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:30.540 line:84%
really how much we're
able to try and translate

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.010 line:84%
from the comics,
and how truthful we

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:37.060 line:84%
try to be true to the
uniqueness and the greatness

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.130 line:90%
of those icons.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:41.030 line:84%
And working with the
filmmakers to do that is--

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.390 line:90%
is a real treat.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:45.870 line:84%
 And you've been here since
the very beginning of Marvel

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.010 line:90%
Studios, is that right?

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.960 line:84%
 Yeah, I was fortunate
enough to get hired

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:50.460 line:90%
by Jon Favreau on Iron Man 1.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:52.830 line:84%
So it was-- design
the Mark I Iron Man

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.343 line:90%
suit, which was a lot of fun.

00:05:54.343 --> 00:05:56.010 line:84%
 I'm just, like, sitting
here with a little piece

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:57.040 line:84%
of Marvel history.
That's you.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:57.840 line:90%
 Oh.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:58.650 line:90%
 That's you.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:05:59.450 line:90%
 That's very kind.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:00.940 line:90%
[LAUGHING]

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:02.370 line:84%
 Thank you so much
for talking with us.

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:03.370 line:90%
 Oh, thank you for having me.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:04.170 line:90%
It's been great.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.330 line:84%
 And you guys, be sure to
go see Spider-Man: Far From

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:08.190 line:90%
Home in theaters on July 2.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:11.540 line:90%
[MUSIC PLAYING]

